    "post-microphysics calc_p_rho_phi recomputes p,al (solve_em4358)"
  ],
  "confirmed_findings": [
    {
      "claim": "alpha=al+alb=ALT represents dry-air specific volume in the moist EOS, independently of use_theta_m.",
      "derivation": "qv=m_v/m_d; a=Rv/Rd; Pi=(p/p0)^(Rd/cp). For theta_m branch, theta_m=theta*(1+a*qv); EOS p=p0[Rd*theta_m/(p0*alpha)]^(cp/(cp-Rd)). For dry-theta branch, the numerator explicitly uses theta*(1+a*qv). In either branch T=theta*Pi gives alpha*p=Rd*T*(1+a*qv)=T*(Rd+Rv*qv), hence rho_d=1/alpha. Hydrostatic branch sets alpha=Rd*theta*(1+a*qv)/p0*(p/p0)^(-cv/cp), yielding the same relation. No-moist branch gives dry EOS. This is more than the generic inverse-density comments.",
      "source_locations": [
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:943",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:1061",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:1114",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:1136",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4830",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:5505",
        "Registry.EM_COMMON:212"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Earlier unsplit physics rho is dry+vapour gas mass density, whereas split microphysics overwrites it with dry-air mass density.",
      "derivation": "Early phy_prep: rho=(1+qv)/ALT. moist_physics_prep_em immediately before microphysics: rho=1/(al+alb), without (1+qv) in either theta branch. They occur at different stages, so this is a definition change, not a same-time recorded density ratio or compression test.",
      "source_locations": [
        "solve_em.F:790",
        "solve_em.F:812",
        "module_first_rk_step_part1.F:219",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4856",
        "solve_em.F:3121",
        "solve_em.F:3822",
        "module_big_step_utilities_em.F:5542",
        "solve_em.F:3881",
        "solve_em.F:3886"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Actual UDM call receives split dry rho through DEN, with no density conversion in the dispatch.",
      "derivation": "solve_em passes RHO=grid%rho, TH=th_phy, P=p_phy, PI=pi_phy. UDM27 dispatch passes DEN=rho, RD=r_d, RV=r_v. rho/DEN are INTENT(IN); temperature starts at TH*PI, pressure and density are copied unchanged to local arrays.",
      "source_locations": [
        "module_microphysics_driver.F:470",
        "module_microphysics_driver.F:2836",
        "module_microphysics_driver.F:2858",
        "module_mp_udm.F:254",
        "module_mp_udm.F:352",
        "module_mp_udm.F:370",
        "module_mp_udm.F:855"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "DEND algebra expects DEN=rho_d+rho_v to return true dry density, not DEN=rho_d.",
      "derivation": "Ideal dry/vapour EOS: p/T=Rd*rho_d+Rv*rho_v, rho_v=qv*rho_d. DEND=(p/T\u2212DEN*Rv)/(Rd\u2212Rv) returns rho_d when DEN=rho_d+rho_v. Substituting source dry DEN=rho_d yields rho_d*[1\u2212Rv/(Rv\u2212Rd)*qv], equal to rho_d only at qv=0. Host constants Rd287/Rv461.6 give coefficient2.643757159221...; native arithmetic/default-real roundoff is separate.",
      "source_locations": [
        "module_mp_udm.F:856",
        "module_microphysics_driver.F:2860",
        "module_model_constants.F:19",
        "module_model_constants.F:22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The mismatch has internal consumers but does not establish a safe global density repair.",
      "derivation": "DEND weights fall-out mass/number transport. DEN also enters slopes, mixing-ratio\u2194volume calculations and activation. For dry-mass mixing ratios, qc*rho_d is already condensate mass per volume. Changing DEN everywhere to moist density would therefore alter other conventions; cannot infer universal repair or calibrated intent from DEND alone.",
      "source_locations": [
        "module_mp_udm.F:2620",
        "module_mp_udm.F:2630",
        "module_mp_udm.F:2636",
        "module_mp_udm.F:2686",
        "module_mp_udm.F:2751",
        "module_mp_udm.F:3115",
        "module_mp_udm.F:2513",
        "module_mp_udm.F:3597"
      ]
    }
  ],
